<article class="env-lemma" id="01OY">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01OY">Lemma <span data-tag="01OY">28.5.4</span>.</a> A locally Noetherian scheme is quasi-separated. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01KO" data-tag="01KO">26.21.6</a> we have to show that the intersection $U \cap V$ of two affine opens of $X$ is quasi-compact. This follows from Lemma <a href="/tag/01OX" data-tag="01OX">28.5.3</a> above on considering the open immersion $U \cap V \to U$ for example. (But really it is just because any open of the spectrum of a Noetherian ring is quasi-compact.) 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>